            {
              "id": "255df1e4-4a9e-46f5-a72f-4e2a5c8b5506",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Appendix N: The Eldritch Roots of Dungeons &amp; Dragons</strong></em> is a collection of essays edited by Peter Bebergal, published by Strange Attractor Press, February 23, 2021."
            },
            {
              "id": "664dce77-2157-4684-b234-d9dd27ece245",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "725059db-230a-419c-9dd5-052783dc8c49",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>An anthology investigating the influences behind </em>Dungeons &amp; Dragons<em>, the most popular modern role-playing game.<br><br>Drawing upon the original list of &quot;inspirational reading&quot; provided by Gary Gygax in the first </em>Dungeon Master's Guide<em>, published in 1979, as well as related periodicals that helped to define the modern role-playing game, </em>Appendix N<em> offers a collection of short fiction and resonant fragments that reveal the literary influences that shaped </em>Dungeons &amp; Dragons<em>, the world's most popular RPG. The stories in </em>Appendix N<em> contextualize the ambitious lyrical excursions that helped set the adventurous tone and dank, dungeon-crawling atmospheres of fantasy roleplay as we know it today.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "fe58e90e-db1c-44f3-91bd-3e59d40ddbdd",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
